        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0329" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857H.01/36</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the French Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daeschner</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12,
                        1925</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of April 7, 1925, in further relation to the question of
                    the adherence of Russia to the Treaty of February 9, 1920, concerning
                    Spitzbergen.</p>
                <p>You state that your Government concurs in the views of this Government that the
                    adherence of Russia to the Treaty should be effected through an agreement
                    calling for ratification, but that it perceives objection to the designation
                    “the regime now functioning in Russia and known as the Union of the Soviet
                    Socialist Republics” which is used in the draft agreement handed to Mr. de
                    Laboulaye by Mr. Grew on July 15, 1924.</p>
                <p>This Government has given careful consideration to the views of the French
                    Government in the matter as expressed in your note of April 7, 1925, and I now
                    enclose a draft of the proposed agreement which it is believed is in harmony
                    with the views of the French Government as set forth in your note.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Grew</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d150-a1.xml" xpointer="d150-a1"/>
